{"diagnosis": "Loopback TX stayed idle so ser_tx from send_pattern[0] at picosoc/simpleuart.v:107 held 1 and RX got 0xff vs want 0xa5 (TRAP: uart data mismatch, tohost FAIL 0xdead). Root cause is picosoc/simpleuart.v:130 `send_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4)` which makes TX bit period ~16x too fast for divider 64, so RX sampling at the configured divider misses the frame. CONE_SLICE picosoc/picosoc.v:190 simpleuart instance agrees on wiring; trace wins.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -127,7 +127,7 @@
 				send_divcnt <= 0;
 			end else
- 			if (send_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4) && send_bitcnt) begin
+ 			if (send_divcnt > cfg_divider && send_bitcnt) begin
 				send_pattern <= {1'b1, send_pattern[9:1]};
 				send_bitcnt <= send_bitcnt - 1;
 				send_divcnt <= 0;", "expected": "tohost PASS (was FAIL 0xdead), TRAP cleared, uart loopback got 0xa5 want 0xa5"}

